## Why This Is Asked
Tests for multi-tenant data isolation are essential even at beginner level. The scenario exercises end-to-end thinking: setup, onboarding flow, and strict cross-tenant boundaries. It also introduces practical trade-offs like environment seeding and mocking external services.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant data isolation
- Test data seeding via API or fixtures
- DNS/subdomain routing mock
- External service mocking (email, auth)
- UI and API assertions for isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright skeleton
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('tenant isolation signup', async ({ page, request }) => {
  await request.post('/api/test/seed-tenant', { data: { name: 'TenantA', subdomain: 'tenant-a' }});
  await page.goto('https://tenant-a.example.com/signup');
  await page.fill('#org-name', 'Tenant A');
  await page.click('#next');
  //... complete 3 onboarding steps
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/tenant-a/);
  // verify isolation
  const res = await request.get('/api/tenant/data', { headers: { 'X-TI-tenant': 'tenant-a' } });
  expect(res.ok()).toBe(true);
  const cross = await request.get('/api/tenant/data', { headers: { 'X-TI-tenant': 'tenant-b' } });
  expect(cross.status()).toBe(403);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you run these tests in parallel across multiple tenants while maintaining isolation?
- How would you validate data isolation after role-based access controls are updated?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design realistic E2E checkout scenarios under network stress, locale shifts, and stock race conditions. It validates understanding of deterministic mocks, proper data isolation, and robust failure handling.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end data seeding with deterministic mocks
- Real-time UI updates across viewports
- Locale and region switching with discount persistence
- Race conditions: stock changes during checkout
- Failure handling, rollback mechanisms, and idempotency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright E2E skeleton
test('checkout with promo code', async ({ page }) => {
  await seedTestData({ locale: 'en-US', promo: 'SAVE20' });
  await page.goto('/cart');

  // Apply promo code
  await page.getByLabel('Promo Code').fill('SAVE20');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Apply' }).click();

  // Verify discount applied
  await expect(page.locator('.discount')).toHaveText('-$20.00');
  await expect(page.locator('.total')).toHaveText('$80.00');

  // Mobile viewport
  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 375, height: 812 });
  await expect(page.locator('.total')).toHaveText('$80.00');

  // Switch locale
  await page.getByLabel('Language').selectOption('de-DE');
  await expect(page.locator('.discount')).toHaveText('-€18,00');

  // Checkout with stock race condition
  await page.goto('/checkout');
  await mockInventoryDecrement();
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Pay' }).click();
  await expect(page.locator('.error')).toContainText('insufficient stock');
